changelog_entry: >-
  Graph revision 18 (`history/v18.patch`, kind graph): performance moves from one
  judgement after serving to the design record and each kernel's own gate. New node
  calibrate_hardware runs a fixed suite on the pinned toolchain as the first device act
  (instruction floors, data movement per access pattern, per-engine rates, the
  throttle ramp and cap under synthetic load, collectives) and writes
  hardware_calibration_record, whose rows name their source; the served shapes per
  requested target are a frozen run input; gate 1 runs the parallelism planner and
  costs every route against entitlement, and the kickoff contract carries a
  performance criterion for every served phase (the target by ratio to entitlement,
  the rest by no regression, an unchanged phase held by program-digest equality) with
  regression_failed reaching backport-route campaigns; the design record carries a
  cost table with a row for every hot op on the design's execution map above one
  registered tolerance, whatever its substrate, an op a chosen form adds costed
  inside its map op's row, each cited to a matching
  calibration row or a device anchor, the roofline being the op's minimum work at the
  binding engine's calibrated rate and a written reason citing floor rows, plus a
  numerics plan per kernel-class increment with oracle regimes, a dtype table, a NaN
  containment note and two refused forms, each kernel-class op's correctness class
  registered so a class change re-presents gate 2, and the user's acceptance of a
  predicted miss recorded as a criterion change (a declined one with no new row or
  form is design_blocked); a kernel-class increment passes on oracle match plus
  kernel_alone ratio; the landed kernels and the block-scoped design re-entries that
  name kernel-class ops are read by retained kernel reviewers sized to the kernels
  in flight, a whole-plan design entry by a fresh challenger, and the whole
  changeset by one seat
  independent of every realizer; review_increment_batch and its re-check go;
  measure_candidate writes the served utilization cap as a calibration row (one file
  per served profile) and re-rates the predicted rows under it into the bundle;
  adjudicate_results splits
  performance_shortfall - any component over its row or served time no row predicted
  - from the residual no_benefit, and routes it back to design, bounded by
  design_blocked on a re-derived row with no new row; review_pr_evidence becomes the
  whole-campaign review with code_findings, and a stale tip at the close-out check
  re-enters the implementation loop; prepare_measurements is a lead-run check on any
  unchanged re-entry; the measurer role names the calibration suite;
  hazards met in a run enter the debt list in four buckets. At the apply gate the
  user's seven-step port workflow was folded in: for a model port the delta trace
  decomposes the forward pass into an op inventory with its kernel gaps, the design
  carries an execution map per served phase as the cost table's subject list and
  holds tests to load-bearing ones, kernel-class increments with distinct ops and
  disjoint surfaces form one kernel set run one seat per item by default from a
  recorded pull list refilled as items finish, with reviewers sized to the items
  in flight, because implementation time is the user's objective, the correctness
  gate is a ladder (coherent generation, benchmark subset with a stated noise form,
  full benchmarks) run in order with later rungs recorded as not run after a
  failure, a maintainer pass over the clean diff and then its delta precedes
  hardware and is re-minted when the diff changes, and the PR carries
  a performance table over the declared context lengths and concurrency levels with
  the accuracy results beside the reference's, from registered bundles, in the
  maintainer's section form (paired numbers at named commits, non-claims stated,
  reproduction per arm, authorship disclosure) that the user named at the apply
  gate; the user's rulings of the same gate keep torch glue inside the bar and the
  bar as the squeeze stop. Evidence:
  the kernel-floor
  reflection record of 2026-10-20 (F1 to F7, W1 to W10, P1 to P13), the replay record
  as folded into reviewer-r18's round-1 list, and the user's decisions of that day,
  the seven-step request at the apply gate included.
  21 nodes, 68 edges, 68 outcomes, 14 checks, 25 evidence definitions; 2425 lines
  become 2820, ceiling 3100 not raised. Release-layer follow-ups listed under EVERY
  COPY: both harness ports of the reviewer, implementer, adjudicator, measurer and
  investigator contracts; SKILL rows; artifact layout with the calibration directory;
  README delegates, counts and two mermaids; VERSION; the workflow test pin; the stop
  guard's batch wording; the queue, schema, queue test and implementer class lists'
  fourth job class; the calibration suite, oracle tooling and hazard list as new
  release items with pinned ceilings.
